WEBVTT

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.630
Wow, what a welcome.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.540
We get back and now we
have to shove off again?

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.830
Give me a break.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.200
Take it up with the aliens.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.920
First alien entering atmosphere.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.460
Heading for northeast sector, Kansas.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.020
Defense level yellow.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.090
All essential personnel to the holding area.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.670
Kansas...

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.220
That's not far.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.200
The target has changed course.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:04.250
What?

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:05.890
Determining direction.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.570
North Dakota, northwest sector.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.830
Inside the red zone,
just next to the dark zone.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:15.730
It can't be.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.470
Lt. Simmons and Lt. Harris
have returned to the base.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.740
I'm worried about the village, but now...

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.680
Yes, we're on our way.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.550
I'm counting on you.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.660
He may just be the only
weapon we have left.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.190
Even you, too.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:39.500
It seems like only yesterday
we were all calling him the EX-1.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:40.970
That's true.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.270
I guess you're right.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.030
Well, about Frank...

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.130
What is it?

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:50.270
He's the only real link we have
between us and the aliens.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.510
If we lose him in the course of the battle...

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.610
But we're closing in on dangerous territory.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.680
Understood.

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.090
"Him"...

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.110
Can you hear me, Frank?

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.370
I hear voice.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.280
Then let's go.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.920
I'll direct regular forces?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.240
What do you mean, General?

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.510
I'm afraid that's our decision.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.180
Our only remaining weapon,
the EX-1, is also an alien.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:11.920
Using it so close to Pilgrimage
Point is too great a risk.

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:14.100
But what would you have Funeral do?

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.400
Don't worry.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.530
You've already accomplished your objectives.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:29.330
Feeding propaganda to civilians,
testing practical weapons...

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:32.680
Even if we halt future development,

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.710
your contributions will survive.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.350
The roses...

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.410
Will the roses really be that beautiful?

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:42.710
What?

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:47.590
So beautiful they'll help you forget
how you're using people as pawns?

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.900
You're brave.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.060
I envy you.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:55.230
I, on the other hand, am merely old.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:57.440
So is this organization.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.500
Someday, you'll be insecure
and take comfort in roses.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.170
What do you mean?

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.110
We all need to cling to something lovely...

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.480
...even if it has thorns.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.240
Why haven't we engaged it yet?

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.880
Relax, Captain Hartland.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:53.460
The anti-alien force Funeral...

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:58.560
and the last secret weapon,
test complex machine EX-1...

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.570
You've done a good job up until now, but...

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:14.410
Colonel Kilgore, we're ready for the attack.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:15.870
Very good.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.560
The Great Wall of China, and
the walled city of Carthage...

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.320
both 17th century walled communities.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:27.910
There's a long tradition of building
walls for protection from enemies.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:34.620
And perhaps this will be
humanity's last great wall.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:48.080
Black SARGs?

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.600
A high-performance SARG model, "TOD."

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.240
Built with stronger alien motors

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.660
and superior maneuverability for combat.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:11.110
Now do you see?

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:15.380
Funeral is no longer the only
agency with anti-alien capabilities.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.310
When did they build those?

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:23.420
Y-Yeah...

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:33.960
Stay cool.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.560
This hasn't been announced publicly yet.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:37.550
Besides...

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.260
I see.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:41.930
So that's it.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:45.200
I get what you were planning.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.430
Taking the name Ryu Soma.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.340
And that price tag...

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.640
As detailed as possible.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:54.200
As simple as you can.

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:58.340
Easy, like writing in a diary.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.790
A little love diary between us.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:08.650
And to keep me quiet, he sent
those black angels of death.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:13.020
Isn't this great, Frank?

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:16.340
Now you don't have to fight.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:18.670
No more fear, no more pain.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:26.250
I was just a pawn the whole time.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:36.350
I could never have even killed you.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:39.890
Transmission from the army HQ.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.550
Security level S.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.660
It's the same IFF codes as the SARGs.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:49.630
Registering SARG types now,
to be known as TODs.

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:59.440
Are these your new roses, General?

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.270
Target remains unchanged.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.570
No sign it is a progressive-type alien.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.700
Very nice.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:29.110
Even the alien seems
impressed by our new toys.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.600
Then let's show it how they work.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.910
Don't attack the brain directly.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:35.310
Gather as much data as possible.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:08.680
What an awful way to attack.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:13.620
I wish I knew what they want
so badly at Pilgrimage Point.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:14.920
I have no idea.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.320
But this...

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.190
...is like a lynching.

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:24.690
How strange.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.300
You're on the aliens' side?

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:28.700
What are you saying?

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:29.760
Hey, Sue.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:33.470
Am I still not allowed to talk to Frank?

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:36.070
Don't come in here, Hattie.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:39.810
Why don't you go out and take a walk?

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.910
Oh, o-okay...

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:50.860
Sentimental...

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:53.350
Maybe so.

00:10:56.850 --> 00:11:01.700
We used to think of him as
a metal monster from space.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.800
But now we've realized
we can communicate with him.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:09.470
But then, someone's after
a thing the aliens dropped

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:12.580
and our fellow humans
are trying to shoot us.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:15.310
I don't understand anything anymore.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:08.100
High-level gravity noise
radiating outside the target.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.480
The alien motor is reacting
far beyond normal levels.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.140
It can't be.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:15.130
Why now?

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:44.640
Target is moving.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:58.350
Target is flying at high speeds.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:01.850
It's outside the range of the TODs' FCS.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.050
Registering as type S-1.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.740
The high-speed type?

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.480
The TODs can't stop it.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.460
Target approaching Pilgrimage Point.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.500
Call the Funeral troops.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:19.340
They want to use Frank?

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.050
That's a formal order.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:23.180
They've got to be kidding.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:27.510
But at this rate, the target
will reach Pilgrimage Point.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:29.440
If it does...

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.750
...it's checkmate.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:32.740
We lose.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.810
So you should ask Frank to help.

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:37.850
No, I'll take care of that.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.530
I'll do it.

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:44.190
Can you hear me, Frank?

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:50.030
You told Hattie to do that?

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:52.400
Of course.

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:54.470
The Earth's in a crisis.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.290
Son of a...

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:02.170
Stop!

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:04.750
Stop that, Sue.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:07.920
I'm going to ask Frank to help us, okay?

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.320
The bad guys are making trouble.

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.690
We can't let them, right?

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:15.760
Hattie...

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.150
Right?

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:22.500
Frank, please...

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:26.120
This might hurt, but stop the bad guys, okay?

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.210
I, stop them...

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:31.630
Yeah, that's right!

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:34.310
We can all go home after that!

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:35.970
All right.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.140
The EX-1 has launched.

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.280
The EX-1 has caught the target.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.050
The target has slowed down!

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:25.760
Put the Mark 303 nuclear warhead into place!

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:27.600
Prepare to launch.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.700
We can burn them to death.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:35.110
Both of them together.

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:43.510
We have visual.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:49.090
He's the final line of defense.

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:10.010
The target's speeding up!

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:11.700
What is this speed?

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:13.740
Frank will be okay, right?

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.280
He can beat the bad guy, right?

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.320
They're right above us.

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.610
The target's crossed the border.

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:57.690
It's too late.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.490
Damn it!

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.220
Checkmate.

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.430
Frank, do your best!

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:07.490
Frank!

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:08.870
That's enough.

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.200
That's enough, Hattie.

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:11.260
But...

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.000
It's okay.

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:15.230
Frank!

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.700
Frank!

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:18.130
Come here!

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.070
Ryu!

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:21.140
Hey!

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:23.710
Lt. Soma!

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.220
I'm not Ryu Soma!

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:40.600
Where are we going?

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:41.900
Hey, Ryu.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:43.160
Call me Takuto!

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:48.120
I was used, tricked into
changing my name to Ryu Soma!

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.360
Damn it!

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.510
I'm at least going to see it
before the world ends!

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:56.070
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:58.780
So you probably want to laugh at me.

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:00.120
Right, Maki?

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:01.260
No!

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:03.040
No, I'm Hattie!

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:03.880
I'm not Maki!

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:04.950
Shut up!

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:06.460
Shut up!

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:09.990
Please show me.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.960
Before it's too late...

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.670
Let me see your smile again...

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:17.890
Ryu...

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:13.860
The target...

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:16.350
...has reached Pilgrimage Point.

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:51.400
Nothing's...

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:52.700
...happening.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.170
That's impossible.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.530
There's no mistake?

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:03.880
The EX-1 and the target are both lost.

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:06.450
Environmental data, all normal.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:08.780
Can't verify if anything is abnormal.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:13.810
Then...

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:16.080
...what is there?

00:20:31.110 --> 00:21:05.390
Frank!

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:07.030
Frank, I'm sorry!

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:08.440
I'm so sorry!

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:13.840
Frank...

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:26.820
Is this your ring?

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.940
Beautiful...

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:45.670
I saw it...

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:48.300
The beautiful...

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:50.470
...land of the fairies.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:55.590
And I came back.

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:06.760
What are you saying, Frank?

00:22:08.540 --> 00:22:10.030
My name is...

00:22:10.340 --> 00:22:14.600
...Yuri.

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:17.440
of the spaceship Odysseus...

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:19.270
...Yuri Leonov.

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:39.070
Like an old Chinese poem...

00:22:39.070 --> 00:22:41.840
Classic songs of the days of yore...

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:44.130
Echoing the anthem of a nation.

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:47.890
Next time,
Awakening and Truth.
